<title>USA: Favorable weather forecast for Brazil coffee belt.</title>
<headline>Favorable weather forecast for Brazil coffee belt.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Near to above-normal temperatures are expected in Brazil through Thursday, with some scattered showers and thunderstorms developing, Weather Services Corp said in an update Tuesday.</p>
<p>The latest indications are for favorable conditions for the trees and the maturing crops. Mostly fair skies were observed this morning, with temperatures averaging near normal from 52F to 59 F (11-15 C), WSC said.</p>
<p>The forecast calls for much colder air to develop over Argentina later this week and pass across Southern Brazil over the weekend.</p>
<p>WSC expects temperatures in Brazil's coffee belt to cool to below normal levels, falling into the 40s to low 50s F (5-12 C) over the weekend, but no damaging cold is expected.</p>
<p>	  ((New York Commodity Desk, 212 859-1640))</p>
